{:id "0026-lab-draft"
 :title "Lab: edits become glyphs with stable identities, and finished words get cues"
 :lupa/area :lab
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "The typing lab knows, for every character of the draft, when it was
        typed and that it is the same character it was a moment ago, however
        the text changed (typing, backspace, paste, editing in the middle).
        Deleted characters linger briefly as ghosts. When a word is finished,
        a cue is placed on exactly its glyphs. All pure: text in, data out."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/lab/draft.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/draft_test.cljc"]
 :design "New namespace halfahead.lab.draft (.cljc, pure). Shapes are in
          halfahead.schema (:ha/draft, :ha/glyph, :ha/ghost, :ha/placed-cue,
          :ha/word-cue); read docs/SCHEMA.md and that file first.

          (empty-draft) -> a valid :ha/draft with empty text.

          (edit draft new-text now-ms cue-fn) -> draft'
            Diff the old and new text by common prefix and common suffix
            (the suffix may not overlap the prefix). Never split a UTF-16
            surrogate pair: move the prefix boundary back, and the suffix
            boundary forward, when either would land inside one. A glyph's
            :char is one UTF-16 unit or one whole surrogate pair.
            - Glyphs in the common prefix and suffix keep their :id and
              :born-ms.
            - Removed glyphs become ghosts {:id :char :died-ms now-ms
              :index <their index in the old text>}.
            - Inserted characters become glyphs with fresh ids from
              :next-id (never reused) and :born-ms now-ms.
            - Ghosts older than 1500 ms at now-ms are dropped.
            - Placed cues keep only glyph ids still present; a cue left with
              none is dropped.
            - Word endings: a word is a maximal run of letters, digits,
              apostrophes (' and ’) and hyphens. A word is finished when the
              character right after it is not a word character. For every
              finished word in the new text whose glyph ids are not all
              already inside one placed cue, call (cue-fn word following)
              where following is the character after the word (a string),
              and place the returned cue at now-ms on that word's glyph ids.
              Words are passed as typed (case preserved). A paste that
              finishes several words cues all of them.
            new-text equal to the old text returns the draft unchanged
            except for ghost pruning.

          (prune draft now-ms) -> draft with ghosts older than 1500 ms
            removed (for frames between edits).

          The result is always a valid :ha/draft (assert in tests)."
 :examples
 ["typing \"hi\" one character at a time from empty: two glyphs, ids 0 and
   1, born at the two times; no cue yet; then \"hi \" cues \"hi\" with
   following \" \" on ids [0 1]"
  "\"hello world\" -> \"hello, world\" (comma inserted at 5): all eleven old
   glyphs keep their ids; one new glyph; the word \"hello\" is now followed
   by \",\" and is cued if it was not already"
  "backspace on \"cat\" -> \"ca\": glyph of \"t\" becomes a ghost with index
   2; the cue on \"cat\" (if any) keeps ids of c and a"]
 :acceptance
 ["Property (test.check, 300+ cases): for any sequence of texts (generated
   from typing, deleting, pasting and replacing, including emoji
   surrogate pairs and newlines), after each edit the glyph chars joined
   equal the text exactly, ids are unique, :next-id exceeds every id ever
   used, and the draft is a valid :ha/draft"
  "Property: glyphs in an unchanged common prefix keep their ids and
   born-ms across an edit"
  "Every example above holds as a test, with a recording cue-fn that
   captures its calls"
  "A paste of \"one two three \" into an empty draft makes three cue-fn
   calls, in order, with following \" \""
  "No surrogate pair is ever split into two glyphs (property over
   emoji-heavy texts)"
  "`bb test` stays green on both hosts"]
 :non-goals
 ["No layout, motion, rendering, DOM, or clock reads (time arrives as
   now-ms); no lookup logic (cue-fn is an argument)"
  "Do not edit halfahead.schema or any other namespace"]
 :context ["src/halfahead/schema.cljc" "docs/SCHEMA.md" "DESIGN.md"
           "src/halfahead/perform.cljc"]
 :budget-usd 10.0}
